    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U18-skill-K-HSK2-form-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 2: form",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Compare temporal words as whole lexical items. A shared character can help recognition but does not make two compounds interchangeable or introduce a new compound.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "之前",
                "pinyin": "zhīqián",
                "meaning": "before; prior to",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "0c019e25cd80e3f2745c36284357399ea8e0612661260373ce16a605d715cdb6"
              },
              {
                "text": "之后",
                "pinyin": "zhīhòu",
                "meaning": "after; afterwards",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "54b3c81c8fa9c33aab3065f2387bb2e7917d908d1888c6c554b186f7a4df8c75"
              },
              {
                "text": "以后",
                "pinyin": "yǐhòu",
                "meaning": "after; later",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "de9df800cf23e88f937d7b72905ad3bad1f6a1e67cdaf4133325b56fa92a8552"
              },
              {
                "text": "请",
                "pinyin": "qǐng",
                "meaning": "to ask; to invite",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "3e785c0ce7e6c5fa2f06f704d64dda4a1e409a8cb9c4bacbec4808f06f56e6fb"
              },
              {
                "text": "睛",
                "pinyin": "jīng",
                "meaning": "eye; eyeball",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "bf3bc97fe7efe01d1098e7fae168e064a69dcb77dfc613a9e2a9a03d742bcbb3"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The temporal expressions mean before, after/afterwards, and after/later. The latter two overlap: neither is an automatically wrong substitute without a narrower context. Also inspect the two already introduced character forms in the comparison; shared parts are imperfect sound or meaning clues.\nFamiliar meanings available: before; prior to; after; afterwards; after; later."
          }
        ]
      },
